{"primary_supplements":[{"finding":"November 2021 introduces function overloads: different total parameter counts, or explicitly typed distinct parameter combinations.","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v5/release-notes/#november-2021","versions":[5]},{"finding":"Required parameter counts and qualified types distinguish definitions; optional parameters, parameter names and return types do not.","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/language/user-defined-functions/#function-overloading","versions":[6]}],"release":"pine-function-overloads-20261030.1","review":{"decisions":["v1-v4 preserve single-definition functions and reject distinct overload declarations.","v5 compares all parameters at declaration; v6 compares required parameters. Calls with equally good headers are ambiguous in both.","Exact argument types precede int-to-float widening. Qualifiers constrain admission without a most-specific-qualifier tie break.","Existing simple/series parameter inference and literal-only default subset remain unchanged.","Resolve concrete definition IDs in Binder; bind explicit expressions once in source order and insert closed defaults afterwards.","Typed IR .12 adds required-parameter masks only for overloaded definitions; runtime validates concrete selected calls without dispatching.","State belongs to each written call chain. Same-name calls within an overload can use earlier definitions; recursion remains forbidden.","Unused bodies receive structural and definite dependency checks; type-dependent overload edges are checked on specialization, including dead branches.","Methods, user-defined reference types and general default expressions remain outside this profile."],"external_execution_verified":false,"test_refs":["tests/test_function_overloads.py","conformance/function-overloads/cases.json"]},"schema_version":"openpine.function-overloads-spec.1","source_lock_sha256":"08a4183d5f9505aac50a6a28164211d3ee94833d4f67af32d8849a630d1b941e","version